  "2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","harness:codex","All-status duplicate check: searched the complete 2,869-item corpus for projection conflict, mutually exclusive selectors and output-include recovery, ran request-specific CLI search, and refreshed live open/in-progress lists. Fully read the new GH-1386 report and live pm-gh1360 metadata and history. Closed GH-1364 repairs scope retention; open GH-1360 owns a broader authority invariant. Neither owns this newly reported global projection-selector repair defect. Preserve their lineage and leave this intake owner open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-06T04:53:44.883Z","harness:codex","Live continuation scope: complete strict corpus 2894/2894 with zero unreadable records, omissions or truncation; selected full metadata and verified complete history read. Deliver composed read ceilings, deliberate-field omission cost, executable projection recovery and prepared source-map/worker privacy repairs in one PR. Only these five owners are active. No duplicate intake created. Auto-release run37414884541 failed specifically on source-map-js before publication; patched lock is part of this delivery."
  "2026-10-06T04:59:39.460Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: original implementation fails the same newly extended primary fixtures before source correction. Combined ceiling resumes refuse read_output_cursor_stale and the positional coordinate is19 where14 is required; explicit status receipts include deliberately excluded children/claim_state; full/global selector recovery repeats its invalid invocation. After correction, original uncapped collection state drives cursor fingerprints and offsets, explicit selectors define receipt scope, and global selector removal preserves command-local mode placement. Real persisted temporary trackers and existing transport matrices own the proof, without new production test seams or duplicate suites. Final full coverage and hosted review remain pending."
  "2026-10-06T05:15:39.904Z","harness:codex","Test audit rationale: extend the existing scoped executable-recovery matrix for global output-include before get, attached output-include after get, and fields/full conflict. Execute the exact emitted argv in the selected tracker with spaces. Parser/quoting unit tests remain distinct transport controls; SDK semantics are not mocked. The first attempted insertion moved a command-local full mode into root position; retain the original caller-selected mode position and consume only competing selectors."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-06T05:31:35.954Z","harness:codex",Recovery argv editing must consume option values and preserve the original command-local mode position. Global selectors may legally precede the command; moving their replacement mode to that global position creates another invalid invocation.
